0..76 Comment "// `Path.step` and `Path.ap` in a type take their types from their operands."
77..79 Comment "//"
80..153 Comment "// A path between paths states its endpoints with these forms, as a paper"
154..227 Comment "// writes them. A wrapper definition that only restates an operand\'s type"
228..252 Comment "// hides that statement."
253..255 Comment "//"
256..324 Comment "// Each declaration states a composite or an action in its own type."
325..327 Comment "//"
328..399 Comment "// - see: #3772 — `Path.step` and `Path.ap` in a type, refused before"
401..473 Comment "/// The action of a function on a path of paths, stated in its own type."
